  "body": "**Stacked on #593** (#555), which is on #573 (#557 + #554). It includes their commits until they merge.\n\n## Root cause of the reopened #330\nThe turn itself was never broken. `pick::lay_on_plane` / `AlignPartToSetup` turn a picked tilted face onto G17/G18/G19 on main, and a new app test pins that. What was broken is what a user could reach on the Setups page. Reproduced through the real shell (1280×720, the block turned 30° about X, real viewport clicks):\n1. **Edge snapping (main):** the plane row armed Edge mode (`plane_pick.rs:31`), so a click on the tilted face took an edge, `check_lay` refused it, and Apply stayed grey. **Already fixed by #573** (7d641c8b, #554: the plane row picks faces only).\n2. **Controls off screen (main and the stack):** the face row was one long line. In the ~285 px properties pane, **Flip, \"Face to plane level\" and Apply fell past the right edge**, so clicks on them did nothing. The only Apply in reach was the Part alignment row's angle Apply, which turns about the bounds centre. That matches the report's \"it only moves the model\". Without a reachable Flip, the default also lays the face's outside up, with the part below the plane.\n\n## What changed\n- **Face row:** split into short lines: label + \"Pick a face\"; plane + Flip; \"Face to plane level\"; the picked face; then **Apply face** on its own line.\n- **Other rows:** the three-points row (#555) and the \"Axes in the plane\" rows (#557) overflowed the same way and got the same treatment.\n- **Not used:** `horizontal_wrapped`, which didn't work because other rows widen the pane's content.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/330-face-lay-rotate.md`.\n- **Maintainer's call:** the default Flip is unchanged: unflipped means the face's outside points along +axis, so a face picked on G17 lays \"outside up\". Many users will expect the picked face to become the bottom, so flipping the default may be worth it.\n- **Not addressed:** the Part alignment row's angle Apply turning about the bounds centre (the \"shifts relative to the origin\" part of the report). Follow-up or maintainer's call.\n\n## How tested\n- **New UI real-click test:** `plane_face_lay::a_clicked_tilted_face_is_turned_flat_onto_g17_not_only_moved`.\n  - It clicks Pick a face → the tilted face in the viewport, asserts Flip, \"Face to plane level\" and Apply face are on screen, then clicks Flip → Apply face.\n  - Result: face normal −Z, face at Z 0, part above. Ctrl+Z restores.\n  - It fails on main (an edge is taken) and on the stack without the layout fix (the Apply click misses).\n- **Structural:** `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure` asserts every option of the face, points and axes rows is inside the window.\n- **App:** `plane_align::a_tilted_face_is_turned_flat_onto_each_plane_with_the_part_above_it` covers G17/G18/G19 with undo. It passes on main too, which pins that the command was right.\n- **Gate:** plane_align, plane_align_edges, points_align, axis_align, setup_align, winding_align, commands_undo and ui lib 385 pass. The headless-GPU test fails only on this machine. Clippy is clean.\n\nChangelog: Setups page \"Lay on a plane\": Flip, \"Face to plane level\" and the row's own \"Apply face\" stay on screen in the properties pane (they ran off its edge), so a picked tilted face can be laid flat on G17/G18/G19; the three-points and axes rows get the same fix (#330)\n\nFixes #330\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
